rows.abstract:
Aims to protect citizens from threats to public health by formulating a program to prevent allergic reactions, respiratory conditions, and other pollen-related respiratory diseases and other health issues among the population.
Proposes to create the Pollen and Mix Mold Monitoring Service under the PAGASA with the following functions (re: pollen grains, mix mold levels, and air pollutants):
a) comprehensive tracking, monitoring, and prediction;
b) accurate/timely information to the public, healthcare, professionals, etc. - to make informed decisions regarding allergies and respiratory illnesses;
c) collection, analysis, and interpretation of data (sources, distribution patterns, and health impacts);
d) collaboration with NGAs, academe, healthcare professionals, etc. - to enhance their understanding;
e) regular updates, forecasts, and alerts through various channels including online platforms and social/traditional media.
